  "result": "Perfect! The foreign currency support is now complete. Let me create a summary:\n\n## Foreign Currency Support Summary\n\n**Added to src/money.js:**\n\n**RATES constant:**\n```javascript\n{\n  EUR: 1,        // Base currency (1 euro per euro)\n  USD: 1.085,    // 1.085 USD per EUR\n  GBP: 0.8425    // 0.8425 GBP per EUR\n}\n```\n\n**New Functions:**\n\n1. **`convert(cents, currency)`**\n   - Converts EUR cents to target currency\n   - Returns `{ok: true, value: cents in target currency}` or `{ok: false, error: 'UNKNOWN_CURRENCY'}`\n   - Uses banker's rounding for fractional cents\n   - Handles negative amounts and zero\n   - Example: `convert(10000, 'USD')` \u2192 `{ok: true, value: 10850}` (100 EUR = 108.50 USD)\n\n2. **`formatMoney(cents, currency)`**\n   - Formats currency amount for display\n   - Currency symbols: `$` (USD), `\u00a3` (GBP), `\u20ac` (EUR), `?` (unknown)\n   - Includes thousands separators with commas\n   - Always 2 decimal places\n   - Examples:\n     - `formatMoney(123456, 'USD')` \u2192 `\"$1,234.56\"`\n     - `formatMoney(-500, 'GBP')` \u2192 `\"-\u00a35.00\"`\n     - `formatMoney(0, 'EUR')` \u2192 `\"\u20ac0.00\"`\n\n**Comprehensive test coverage (23 new tests):**\n- Exchange rate verification\n- Currency conversion (EUR \u2194 USD, EUR \u2194 GBP)\n- Unknown currency rejection with proper error\n- Zero and negative amount handling\n- Banker's rounding during conversion\n- Formatting for all supported currencies\n- Negative amount formatting\n- Thousands separator and decimal formatting\n- Integration tests combining convert + formatMoney\n- Edge cases (very large amounts, single cents)\n\n**Test results:** All 393 tests pass (370 previous + 23 new currency tests)\n\nThe system now supports invoicing in multiple currencies while maintaining internal EUR cent precision, with proper rounding and human-friendly formatting for each currency.",
